  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) or shows early negative signals.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp upward spikes in price (especially after 70+ peaks).",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if 3-5 consecutive days show high forecast error, reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10%.",
    "Increase downward bias when historical 30-day mean is below 65.0 and true outcome is consistently below 65.0.",
    "Correct for lag: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast, adjust next forecast downward by 3-5% to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "When sentiment is neutral or positive (sentiment = 0), maintain forecast stability but add 1-2% downward buffer if recent true outcomes are trending down."
  ]
}
